class.description:
A one-shot timer managed by the scene tree, which emits [signal timeout] on completion. See also [method Stage.create_timer].
As opposed to [Timer], it does not require the instantiation of a node. Commonly used to create a one-shot delay timer as in the following example:
[codeblocks]
[csharp]
public async Task SomeFunction()
{
	Orb.Print("Timer started.");
	await ToSignal(GetStage().CreateTimer(1.0f), StageTimer.SignalName.Timeout);
	Orb.Print("Timer ended.");
}
[/csharp]
[/codeblocks]
The timer will be dereferenced after its time elapses. To preserve the timer, you can keep a reference to it. See [RefCounted].
[b]Note:[/b] The timer is processed after all of the nodes in the current frame, i.e. node's [method Entity._frame] method would be called before the timer (or [method Entity._step] if [code]process_in_physics[/code] in [method Stage.create_timer] has been set to [code]true[/code]).
